# Counter-example (ONE violation): a lang:Paraphrase that names no lang:paraphraseSamenessKind
# (sh:minCount 1 on lang:ParaphraseKindShape) → lang:UndeclaredParaphraseKind. A paraphrase
# with no declared sameness kind claims an equivalence without saying which corner of the
# Frege triangle — denotation, sense, or force-and-content — it holds fixed, smuggling in an
# equivalence without content. The paraphrased form is a fully-situated English composed
# form, so ONLY the MinCount finding fires.

@prefix lang:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/lang/> .

ex:english a lang:SignSystem .

ex:origClause a lang:ComposedForm ; lang:inSignSystem ex:english .
ex:plainClause a lang:ComposedForm ; lang:inSignSystem ex:english .

ex:paraNoKind a lang:Paraphrase ;
    lang:paraphraseOf ex:origClause ;
    lang:paraphraseForm ex:plainClause .
